  "source_interpretation": {
    "conclusion": "UNKNOWN is supported: the complete captured TOGO source supplies the named preparation and receiving dose but neither establishes a closed buffer list nor explicitly identifies omitted buffer constituents. The separately listed main water and salts stock must not be imported as buffer carrier evidence. MediaDive J209 offers the same attributed recipe and a flattened salts representation, not an independent printed buffer formula.",
    "enum": {
      "description": "Completeness of a component decomposition relative to its cited source.",
      "permissible_values": {
        "COMPLETE": {
          "description": "The source explicitly establishes that the listed constituents are complete."
        },
        "PARTIAL": {
          "description": "The source explicitly indicates that additional constituents are omitted."
        },
        "UNKNOWN": {
          "description": "The source does not establish whether the list is complete."
        }
      }
    },
    "positive_observations": [
      "TOGO M202 components[0].items[3] names 4% Na2CO3--CO2 buffer, added at 100 ml to the receiving medium. This does not establish stock final volume or concentration basis.",
      "The complete TOGO capture has a main solution and a separate seven-item Salts solution. Its main water 430 ml and salts water 100 ml are not a carbonate-buffer recipe.",
      "TOGO pH 6.7-6.8 and MediaDive J209 pH information concern the receiving medium. They do not establish stock pH or CO2 equilibration endpoint.",
      "MediaDive J209 recipe[11] names compound1685 with attribute4% and amount100 ml. The ingredient1685 registry links J209. Its generic carbonate annotations do not establish exact identity of the whole preparation.",
      "No source-explicit omitted carbonate-buffer constituent is identified in these complete captured objects; absence of carrier/basis knowledge does not meet the native PARTIAL definition."
    ],
    "retained_association": "The positive ingredient1685→J209/M98-5→JCM209 and TOGO M202/JCM_M209 chain remains intact. Completeness correction does not reject that source association or require another stock owner.",
    "retained_unknowns": [
      "percentage basis",
      "solvent/carrier",
      "carbonate hydration/supplied form",
      "CO2 dose and equilibration endpoint",
      "stock pH",
      "stock final volume"
    ],
    "no_new_primary_http_retrieval": true,
    "failed_direct_jcm_retrieval": "Retained as unsuccessful context; not used as positive source proof."
  },
  "exact_change_assessment": {
    "payload": "Whole-object and raw YAML rollback to the authentic predecessor is exact after restoring PARTIAL and removing the one appended truthful AI-assisted history event. LABEL_ENUMERATION, both UNMAPPED named parts, MappingEvidence LLM_SUGGESTION, ComponentEvidence, all original history, identifiers, aliases, quantities, source notes and unknowns are unchanged.",
    "history_event": {
      "timestamp": "2026-11-08T08:15:57.825458+00:00",
      "curator": "Codex worker10 /root",
      "action": "CORRECTED_COMPONENT_COMPLETENESS",
      "changes": "Issue #1201, W10-SV2-INHERITED-COMPLETENESS-001 / SCI-CARBONATE-COMPLETENESS-001: changed only component_assertion.completeness from PARTIAL to UNKNOWN. The complete captured TOGO M202 recipe names the stock and its receiving amount but does not establish stock-list closure or explicitly omitted stock constituents. Preserved LABEL_ENUMERATION, both source-named UNMAPPED parts, LLM_SUGGESTION mapping evidence, original sources and history, and the exact case21/187 source association. Solvent, percentage basis, carbonate hydration, CO2 dose/endpoint, stock pH, supplied form and final volume remain unknown; no water or composition is inferred. No identity, role, whole-owner or export approval change. Filed finding: https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1201#issuecomment-6719089745",
      "previous_status": "MAPPED",
      "new_status": "MAPPED",
      "llm_assisted": true
    },
    "dependent_metadata": "Only cases21/187 and the one selected proposal differ in author-core. Original source case applicability, raw labels, routing, dispositions and case/proposal backlinks remain exact. The case21/proposal quantitative hold now says UNKNOWN. Existing C002 stock_payload_unchanged and provenance_successor assertions remain historical, with an explicit current completeness_successor bridge.",
    "review_at_author_freeze": "Both cases and the proposal correctly remained pending until this separate review. Their exact earlier review objects are retained in the successor marker.",
